---
import LegalPage from './LegalPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../lib/site';
import { localePath, useTranslations, type Locale } from '../../i18n';

/**
 * The English privacy policy.
 *
 * A translation of `PrivacyDe.astro`, not a different policy: the controller
 * is established in Germany, so the law described here is the GDPR and the
 * TDDDG, and the legal bases are cited rather than paraphrased away. The
 * German version is the authoritative one, and any change to the facts — a
 * new service, a new stored value — has to be made in both.
 */
const LOCALE: Locale = 'en';
const t = useTranslations(LOCALE);

const GITHUB_PRIVACY =
  'https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement';
const GMX_PRIVACY = 'https://www.gmx.net/datenschutz/';
---

<LegalPage
  locale={LOCALE}
  title={t.legal.privacyTitle}
  description={t.legal.privacyDescription}
  heading={t.legal.privacyTitle}
  lede={t.legal.privacyLede}
  closingDate
>
  <p>
    LCR Labs is operated from Germany, so this policy describes processing under the GDPR and
    German law. It is an English translation of the{' '}
    <a href={localePath('/privacy/', 'de')}>German version</a>, which is the authoritative one.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Privacy at a glance</h2>
  <h3>General information</h3>
  <p>
    Protecting your personal data matters to us. The following notes give an overview of which
    personal data is processed when you visit this website, and for what purposes.
  </p>
  <p>Personal data is any data by which you can be personally identified.</p>
  <p>
    The LCR Labs website is designed as a data-minimising static information site. No user
    accounts are kept, and no payment, purchase or customer data is processed through it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Technically necessary data may nevertheless be processed, in particular by the hosting
    provider. Beyond that, personal data is processed if you choose to contact LCR Labs.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Controller</h2>
  <p>The controller within the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:</p>
  <address class="address">
    <strong>Luca Runkel</strong><br />
    Bahnhofstraße 12<br />
    79353 Bahlingen<br />
    Germany
  </address>
  <p>
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    The controller decides, alone or jointly with others, on the purposes and means of
    processing personal data on this website.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Hosting via GitHub Pages</h2>
  <p>This website is served by GitHub Pages.</p>
  <p>The providers are in particular:</p>
  <address class="address">
    <strong>GitHub B.V.</strong><br />
    Prins Bernhardplein 200<br />
    1097 JB Amsterdam<br />
    Netherlands
  </address>
  <p>and, as part of the GitHub infrastructure:</p>
  <address class="address">
    <strong>GitHub, Inc.</strong><br />
    88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street<br />
    San Francisco, CA 94107<br />
    USA
  </address>
  <p>
    When a website served by GitHub Pages is requested, GitHub logs the visitor's IP address in
    particular and stores it for security reasons.
  </p>
  <p>
    In the course of providing the GitHub services, further technical usage and connection data
    may be processed, for example information about the browser or device used and the time and
    technical characteristics of a request.
  </p>
  <p>
    This processing is necessary in order to provide the website technically and to ensure the
    security, stability and functioning of the service.
  </p>
  <p>
    Insofar as the processing falls within our area of responsibility, it is based on
    Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest lies in providing this website securely,
    reliably and economically.
  </p>
  <p>
    GitHub also processes data outside the European Union, in particular in the United States.
    GitHub states that it uses appropriate safeguards for such international transfers,
    including the European Commission's standard contractual clauses, and that it participates
    in the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework.
  </p>
  <p>
    Further information about the processing of data by GitHub is available in{' '}
    <a href={GITHUB_PRIVACY} rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's official privacy statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Encrypted transmission</h2>
  <p>This website is served over HTTPS.</p>
  <p>
    The connection between your browser and the website is therefore encrypted, so that data
    exchanged during transmission cannot readily be read by third parties.
  </p>
  <p>
    An encrypted connection is usually recognisable by the website's address beginning with{' '}
    <code>https://</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Server and access data</h2>
  <p>Technically necessary connection data arises when this website is requested.</p>
  <p>This may include the IP address in particular.</p>
  <p>
    Such technical data is processed solely in order to deliver the website, to ensure its
    technical stability and to detect or prevent misuse and security attacks.
  </p>
  <p>
    LCR Labs does not combine this technical access data with other data sources for
    advertising, analytics or profiling purposes. LCR Labs has no access to the raw server logs
    of this website.
  </p>
  <p>
    Insofar as this processing falls within our area of responsibility, the legal basis is
    Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest lies in the secure and trouble-free operation
    of the website.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cookies, tracking and web analytics</h2>
  <p>
    As matters stand, LCR Labs uses no analytics, advertising or tracking services on this
    website and creates no personal usage profiles.
  </p>
  <p>
    In particular, no services such as Google Analytics, Google Ads, Meta Pixel or comparable
    tracking technologies are used.
  </p>
  <p>
    LCR Labs sets no cookies that are not technically necessary. Accordingly, no consent or
    cookie banner is currently required for such services.
  </p>

  <h3>Locally stored preferences</h3>
  <p>
    This website stores two settings in your browser's local storage
    (<code>localStorage</code>) — and only if you make the choice in question explicitly:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>lcr-theme</code>, with the value <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code>, once you
      use the light or dark appearance control in the header.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>lcr-language</code>, with the value <code>en</code> or <code>de</code>, once you use
      the language control in the header.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Both values remain on your device, in your browser, and are not transmitted to LCR Labs or
    to any third party. They contain nothing but the interface preference you explicitly chose,
    and are not used for analytics, advertising or profiling purposes, nor to recognise
    visitors.
  </p>
  <p>
    Without such an explicit choice nothing is stored: the appearance then follows your
    operating system's setting, and the language follows solely from the address you requested.
    There is no automatic redirect based on a stored language or on the language configured in
    your browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    This storage serves to provide a service you have explicitly requested and is therefore
    strictly necessary within the meaning of § 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG; no consent is required for
    it. You can delete the stored values at any time through your browser's settings.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Contact by email</h2>
  <p>
    This website contains no contact, support or upload form. Contact is made exclusively by
    email to the address given above.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you contact LCR Labs by email, the personal data you transmit is processed. This may
    include in particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your email address</li>
    <li>your name, if you provide it</li>
    <li>the content of your message</li>
    <li>any attachments or further details you choose to send</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The data is used solely in order to deal with your enquiry and to communicate with you.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your enquiry relates to the initiation or performance of a contractual relationship, the
    processing is based on Article 6(1)(b) GDPR.
  </p>
  <p>
    For other enquiries, the processing is based on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate
    interest lies in dealing with and answering incoming enquiries appropriately.
  </p>
  <p>
    The transmitted data is deleted once the enquiry in question has been dealt with
    conclusively and no statutory retention obligations or other legitimate grounds for further
    storage exist.
  </p>

  <h2>8. GMX email service</h2>
  <p>LCR Labs uses an email service provided by GMX for email communication.</p>
  <p>GMX is a service of:</p>
  <address class="address">
    <strong>1&amp;1 Mail &amp; Media GmbH</strong><br />
    Zweigniederlassung Karlsruhe<br />
    Brauerstraße 48<br />
    76135 Karlsruhe<br />
    Germany
  </address>
  <p>
    If you contact LCR Labs by email, the data required to deliver and store the message is
    also processed technically on the email provider's systems. This concerns in particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>sender and recipient address</li>
    <li>technical email metadata</li>
    <li>the content of the message</li>
    <li>any attachments</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Further information about the processing of personal data by GMX is available in{' '}
    <a href={GMX_PRIVACY} rel="noopener noreferrer">GMX's official privacy information</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. External links</h2>
  <p>
    This website may contain links to external websites, for example to the privacy information
    of the providers named in this policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you follow such an external link, you leave the area of responsibility of this website.
    The external provider's own privacy terms then apply to any subsequent processing of
    personal data.
  </p>
  <p>
    LCR Labs has no influence over the data processing carried out by the operator of an
    external website once it has been opened. The external provider is contacted only when you
    actively click such a link.
  </p>

  <h2>10. External fonts and content</h2>
  <p>
    When this website is opened normally, LCR Labs embeds no external fonts, advertising
    networks or third-party social media plugins that would establish a connection to those
    third parties as the page loads.
  </p>
  <p>
    The fonts already present on your device are used for display; images, styles and scripts
    are delivered exclusively by this website itself.
  </p>
  <p>
    The German and the English version of this website are pre-built static pages. No external
    translation or localisation service is used for switching languages, and no text or
    language input is transmitted to third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Storage period</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data is stored, as a rule, only for as long as is necessary for the respective
    purpose of processing.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the purpose of the processing ceases to apply, the data concerned is deleted, unless
    statutory retention obligations or other legally permissible grounds for further storage
    exist.
  </p>
  <p>
    Technical log data processed directly by hosting or infrastructure providers may be subject
    to those providers' own storage and deletion periods.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Legal bases for processing</h2>
  <p>
    Insofar as personal data is processed on this website, this is done in particular on the
    following legal bases:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Article 6(1)(b) GDPR</strong> — where processing is necessary for the performance
      of a contract or for pre-contractual measures.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Article 6(1)(f) GDPR</strong> — where processing is necessary to protect
      legitimate interests, in particular for the secure technical operation of the website or
      for dealing with general enquiries.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Article 6(1)(a) GDPR</strong> — where consent is expressly obtained for a
      particular processing operation.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Consent once given can be withdrawn at any time with effect for the future.</p>

  <h2>13. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Subject to the statutory conditions, you have in particular the following rights with
    regard to your personal data:
  </p>

  <h3>Right of access — Article 15 GDPR</h3>
  <p>
    You can request information as to whether, and which, personal data concerning you is
    processed.
  </p>

  <h3>Right to rectification — Article 16 GDPR</h3>
  <p>
    You can request the rectification of inaccurate personal data or the completion of
    incomplete personal data.
  </p>

  <h3>Right to erasure — Article 17 GDPR</h3>
  <p>
    Subject to the statutory conditions, you can request the erasure of your personal data.
  </p>

  <h3>Right to restriction of processing — Article 18 GDPR</h3>
  <p>
    Subject to the statutory conditions, you can request that the processing of your personal
    data be restricted.
  </p>

  <h3>Right to data portability — Article 20 GDPR</h3>
  <p>
    Where the statutory conditions are met, you can receive personal data you have provided in
    a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format, or request that it be transmitted
    to another controller.
  </p>

  <h3>Right to object — Article 21 GDPR</h3>
  <p>
    Where personal data is processed on the basis of Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, you can object to
    that processing at any time on grounds relating to your particular situation.
  </p>

  <h3>Withdrawal of consent — Article 7(3) GDPR</h3>
  <p>
    Consent already given can be withdrawn at any time with effect for the future. The
    lawfulness of processing carried out up to the withdrawal remains unaffected.
  </p>

  <p>
    To exercise your rights, you can contact LCR Labs at the email address given above,{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority</h2>
  <p>
    If you consider that the processing of your personal data infringes data protection law,
    you have the right under Article 77 GDPR to lodge a complaint with a data protection
    supervisory authority.
  </p>
  <p>For Baden-Württemberg, the competent authority includes:</p>
  <address class="address">
    <strong>
      Der Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit Baden-Württemberg
    </strong><br />
    Heilbronner Straße 35<br />
    70191 Stuttgart<br />
    Germany
  </address>
  <p>
    Email: <a href="mailto:poststelle@lfdi.bwl.de">poststelle@lfdi.bwl.de</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    The right to contact another competent data protection supervisory authority remains
    unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Automated decision-making and profiling</h2>
  <p>
    No automated decision-making, including profiling, within the meaning of Article 22 GDPR
    takes place through this website.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Within the bounds of what is technically and economically reasonable, LCR Labs takes
    appropriate measures to protect personal data against loss, misuse, unauthorised access and
    unauthorised alteration.
  </p>
  <p>The website is transmitted encrypted over HTTPS in particular.</p>
  <p>
    Despite appropriate security measures, absolute protection cannot be guaranteed for data
    transmission over the internet.
  </p>

  <h2>17. Changes to this privacy policy</h2>
  <p>
    This privacy policy may be adapted if the website, the services used or the legal
    requirements change.
  </p>
  <p>The current version published on this website applies.</p>
  <p>
    The provider identification is set out in the{' '}
    <a href={localePath('/imprint/', LOCALE)}>legal notice</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
